(Apologies to anyone who might be getting this the second time, I have
had a few email problems).

As I thought I needed one of these for the driver I am trying to write
for sound on the Dreamcast, and as I couldn't see one anywhere else, I
have set up a small cross reference (using lxr) for the ALSA lib and
utils code.

It is at http://newgolddream.dyndns.info/lxr/source

Please be gentle - it's at the wrong end of an ADSL line. If the address
fails to resolve please email me here (the auto-update on my commodity
router no longer seems to be working).

I hope this is of use to kernel developers in the same position as me,
as well as to ALSA developers.

NB: Due to a bug in the lxr perl alsa-lib has had to be renamed alsa_lib
and alsa-utils alsa_utils. Any other bug information gratefully
received.

Adrian McMenamin





